ame":"SHOUT!","title":"Stand Up for “Shout”","subtitle":"University of Oregon events and games · Eugene, Oregon","notes":"When “Shout” starts, join the crowd in the Duck anthem; the university links its campus history to Animal House, filmed at UO in 1978.","short_summary":"A crowd-singalong anthem tied directly to UO’s Animal House history.","evidence_claim":"UO identifies “Shout” as a Duck anthem and notes that Animal House was filmed on the UO campus in 1978.","source_url":"https://www.uoregon.edu/uo-traditions","source_title":"UO Traditions","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Occurs as programmed at university and athletics events.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"uo-throw-your-o","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Throw Your O","title":"Throw Your O","subtitle":"University of Oregon community · Eugene, Oregon","notes":"Form an O with your hands to signal Oregon pride; it began as an Oregon Marching Band cue when Autzen was too loud for spoken direction.","short_summary":"A hand sign whose origin is rooted in the Oregon Marching Band.","evidence_claim":"OregonNews reports that band director Steven Paul created the O hand signal in the 1980s as a cue to play “Mighty Oregon.”","source_url":"https://news.uoregon.edu/oq/o-the-places-you-will-go","source_title":"O the Places You Will Go","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2016-11-01","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"A gesture used across UO community and athletics settings.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"uo-duck-friday","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Duck Friday","title":"Wear Green and Yellow on Duck Friday","subtitle":"University of Oregon community · Eugene, Oregon","notes":"Wear UO green and yellow on Friday, then share your school-spirit look with #DuckFriday if you want to join the public ritual.","short_summary":"A weekly UO color-wearing tradition connecting Ducks on and off campus.","evidence_claim":"University Communications encourages Ducks to wear green and yellow on Fridays and calls the practice Duck Friday.","source_url":"https://communications.uoregon.edu/duck-friday","source_title":"Duck Friday","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Participation is informal and does not require an event ticket.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"uo-mighty-oregon","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Mighty Oregon","title":"Learn “Mighty Oregon”","subtitle":"University of Oregon athletics and band tradition · Eugene, Oregon","notes":"Listen for the school fight song at Duck events and learn its refrain; UO says it was first performed on March 4, 1916.","short_summary":"The university’s century-plus-old fight-song tradition.","evidence_claim":"OregonNews states that “Mighty Oregon” was first performed March 4, 1916 and continues as UO’s anthem.","source_url":"https://news.uoregon.edu/content/new-mighty-oregon-t-shirts-raise-money-marching-band","source_title":"New 'Mighty Oregon' T-shirts raise money for marching band","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2016-09-09","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Performed at applicable athletics and Oregon Marching Band appearances.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
